From 64b708cb449e2472e700a6787107f99e45ea6364 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Advait Johari <zakethegr8@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 16:42:30 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] fix(browser): undo what the connection prompt does to the
 desktop

Attaching to an existing profile makes Chromium show "Allow remote debugging?".
To show it, Chromium restores a minimized browser window, the prompt takes the
foreground, and closing it activates the browser window. So the user's
minimized browser came back on screen and their focus moved to it.

Preparation now reads the desktop state before it connects and restores it
after, success or not: it minimizes the window again without activating it,
and if the browser still holds the foreground it hands it back to the window
that had it. A user who switched apps meanwhile is left alone.

When an attempt fails, the prompt it showed stays open but can no longer
connect anything, and once the window is minimized again nobody can see it.
Every later attempt then found two prompts and refused. Failed attempts now
deny the prompts left open on the window by closing them, which Chromium treats
as Cancel. Prompts are matched to their windows by exact title among the
windows the browser window owns, so its other popups stay open.
